# Configurando FeignClient com Timeout e Conexões Máximas

## 1. Classe de Configuração Feign

```java
import io.github.openfeign.ClientConfig;
import io.github.openfeign.FeignBuilder;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Value;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;
import java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;

@Configuration
public class FeignConfig {

    @Value("${feign.httpclient.max-connections:10}")
    private int maxConnections;

    @Value("${feign.httpclient.connect-timeout:3000}")
    private int connectTimeout;

    @Value("${feign.httpclient.read-timeout:5000}")
    private int readTimeout;

    @Bean
    public FeignClientFactoryBean feignClientFactoryBean() {
        return new FeignClientFactoryBean();
    }

    // Opcional: Configuração customizada do FeignClient
    @Bean
    public ClientConfig clientConfig() {
        return new ClientConfig.Builder()
                .options(new Options()
                        .connectTimeout(connectTimeout)
                        .readTimeout(readTimeout))
                .build();
    }
}
```

## 2. Propriedades de Configuração (application.yml)

```yaml
spring:
  cloud:
    openfeign:
      client:
        config:
          default:
            connect-timeout: 3000
            read-timeout: 5000
            max-connections: 10
            max-wait: 1000
```

Ou em **application.properties**:

```properties
spring:
  cloud:
    openfeign:
      client:
        config:
          default:
            connect-timeout: 3000
            read-timeout: 5000
            max-connections: 10
            max-wait: 1000
```

## 3. Cliente Feign com Timeout

```java
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.GetMapping;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;
import io.github.openfeign.chunked.ChunkedResponse;
import java.time.Duration;

@RestController
public class MyServiceClient {

    private final MyApiService apiService;

    public MyServiceClient(MyApiService apiService) {
        this.apiService = apiService;
    }

    @GetMapping("/data")
    public String getData() {
        return apiService.fetchData();
    }
}

interface MyApiService {
    @GetMapping("/data")
    String fetchData();
}
```

## 4. Cliente Feign Customizado

```java
import io.github.openfeign.FeignClient;
import io.github.openfeign.Request;
import io.github.openfeign.Response;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Value;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@FeignClient(name = "myService", url = "${feign.service.url}")
public interface MyApiService {

    @GetMapping("/data")
    Response fetchData();

    @PostMapping("/data")
    Response postData(@RequestBody String body);
}
```

## Resumo das Propriedades Disponíveis

| Propriedade | Descrição | Valor Padrão |
|-------------|-----------|--------------|
| `max-connections` | Número máximo de conexões | 10 |
| `connect-timeout` | Tempo de conexão em ms | 3000 |
| `read-timeout` | Tempo de leitura em ms | 5000 |
| `max-wait` | Tempo de espera por resposta | 1000 |

## Dependência Maven

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-cloud-starter-openfeign</artifactId>
</dependency>
```

Essa configuração permite que você controle finamente o comportamento de conexão e timeout dos seus clientes Feign dentro do Spring Boot!

